Title: Chelsea win Club World Cup: Donald Trump stays on stage with players for trophy lift
Date: 2025-07-14
Firsthand information: {'Speaker': [{'Speaker': 'Reece James', 'Text': 'They told me that he was going to present the trophy and then exit the stage, and I thought that he was going to exit the stage, but he wanted to stay.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 4, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 130}}, {'Speaker': 'Reece James', 'Text': 'He just congratulated me and the team for lifting the trophy and told us to enjoy the moment.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 5, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 80}}, {'Speaker': 'Cole Palmer', 'Text': "I knew he was going to be here but I didn't know he was going to be on the stand when we lifted the trophy.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 6, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 94}}, {'Speaker': 'Cole Palmer', 'Text': 'I was a bit confused, yes.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 7, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 25}}, {'Speaker': 'Donald Trump', 'Text': 'having a really great time', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 10, 'StartChar': 117, 'EndChar': 144}}, {'Speaker': 'Donald Trump', 'Text': "Gianni is a friend of mine, he's done such a great job with the league and with soccer - or as they would call it 'football', but I guess we call it soccer. I'm not sure that change could be made very easily.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 11, 'StartChar': 35, 'EndChar': 194}}, {'Speaker': 'Donald Trump', 'Text': "But it's great to watch - and this is a little bit of an upset that we're watching today, isn't it?", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 12, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 91}}, {'Speaker': 'Donald Trump', 'Text': 'I think we could do that. I think I could do that.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 14, 'StartChar': 97, 'EndChar': 143}}], 'Description': [{'Description': "Following the Blues' 3-0 win over Paris St-Germain in New Jersey on Sunday, Trump presented the trophy to Chelsea captain Reece James before being invited to move aside by Fifa president Gianni Infantino.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 2, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 178}}, {'Description': 'However, Trump remained alongside James and goalkeeper Robert Sanchez, and applauded as James lifted the trophy - staying in position for a few seconds before he and Infantino left at the rear of the stage.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 3, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 199}}, {'Description': 'Trump watched Chelsea\'s impressive victory in the final alongside Infantino and said in an interview with Dazn at half-time that he was "having a really great time".', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 10, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 144}}, {'Description': 'In a longer interview broadcast later on Sunday, he added: "Gianni is a friend of mine, he\'s done such a great job with the league and with soccer - or as they would call it \'football\', but I guess we call it soccer. I\'m not sure that change could be made very easily.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 11, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 194}}, {'Description': 'When it was suggested he could make an executive order so that the sport was referred to as "football" from now on, Trump smiled and said: "I think we could do that. I think I could do that."', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 14, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 143}}], 'Image': []}
